    "Notes Updated": "5/8/2024",
    "Scouting Notes": "Reliever most likely\n 2S with 20+ inches of run, sitting 91 93 can get a little higher\n Changeup is an airbender type of pitch, absolutely filthy\n Curve is a really solid pitch as well\n Also throwing an upper 80's cutter\n Command and control have both been good\n Could be a legit star reliever",
    "Notes Updated 2": "7/12/2023",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Draft Report\nAnother pitcher that I was tracking as a potential Brewers pick. He seemed like an arm that an analytical front office would love and the Brewers have been great with a profile like his. Yoho is relatively new to pitching full  time, as he was a two way early in his college career. He’s been hurt a number of times and despite being 23 years old, he somehow has three (!) years of eligibility left and was committed to transfer to Arkansas next year. It sounds as though he will sign though, and I find that to be pretty exciting.  According to BAseball America, “Yoho’s high  70s changeup has a ton of late fade and tumble, is an effective pitch against both right and left handed hitters, and had an impressive 61% miss rate. His sweeping slider had a 56% miss rate, while his curveball has big time depth and a 62% miss rate.” While Yoho was used as a reliever at Indiana and that was the plan at Arkansas as well. I’m not entirely convinced that he shouldn’t be given a shot at starting in pro ball. He definitely has a starters repertoire. It will likely come down to durability and whether the Brewers believe he can handle a starters workload. Yoho is an older pick, but a four pitch pitcher with this kind of stuff and solid command to go with it, is not commonly available in the 8th round.",
